## Implementation surface

- `parse::codex::Parser<R: BufRead + Seek>` is a bounded reader, not an all-session
  collector. The caller supplies the IR-owned SessionId; source/native identity,
  cwd, git, CLI version and timestamps come from session_meta. Parser revision 1.
- `next_record()` returns a batch for one native line. A batch is atomic for the
  cursor: consume all derived compaction messages before checkpointing. Persist
  both Session and Cursor; reapply the without_raw option when restoring that
  run mode. The cursor stores offset, line ordinal, next seq, prior id, turn and
  parse-error count. Partial tail bytes are deliberately reread after append.
- User/assistant/developer/system messages, inline image content hashes,
  readable/sealed reasoning, function/custom calls and their outputs, explicit
  task/turn starts/ends/abort, token_count usage, notices and context map to IR.
  Compaction replacement messages get derived ids and remain separate from the
  sealed compaction; their retained parent record is emitted only once on replay.
- A tool output's call_id is a reference to its call rather than its own id.
  Its own id or native ordinal is used, so call and output do not collide.
- `Sealed.provider` is `Provider::Codex`, as required by the existing lc-ir
  Provider enum. The brief's OpenAI label denotes the native API format; no
  nonexistent Openai IR variant or breaking CBOR change was introduced.
- Per lc-ir §3, token_usage_record, world_state and communication metadata are
  opaque Native records; typed Usage comes from event_msg/token_count. Future
  unrecognized items are Unknown. All retained raw bytes remain replayable.
- `lower::codex::write` writes to a caller-owned Write, opens no native client
  directory/database, checks dense order and metadata first, and returns typed
  I/O errors for unsupported input. It does not buffer/sort an entire session.
- Added base64 0.22.1 to decode inline image bodies for BlobRef hashes; the deny
  check passes across 53 direct/transitive/dev packages. Remote images are not
  fetched and get Unknown blocks with original URI retained in raw.
- Tests/support fixtures are authored synthetic Rust values; no real log was
  read or included. tests/support/p0_mock.py copies the project's pinned P0
  helper, retaining its header and an exact source credit. Its child environments
  are allowlisted, with private HOME/CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/CODEX_HOME/XDG directories,
  dummy keys, local mock endpoints and closed external proxy settings. Python
  bytecode output is disabled. Native client calls have 25-second deadlines.

## Verification scope and limits

- `cargo test --offline --locked --test codex --test codex_resume`: exit 0,
  nine codec tests plus one process test, zero failures. The process test's two
  candidate verdicts are actual CLI/model-request observations, not stdout text
  claims. An absent CLI is labelled SKIP; the installed CLI ran in this gate.
- `make test`: exit 0. `cargo clippy --offline --locked --all-targets
  --all-features -- -D warnings`, headers, secrets and deny also ran directly
  with exit 0 during development. `git diff --check` exited 0.
- Stale-receipt control: immediately after the report commit,
  `make check-formal-evidence` exited 2 with stale formal source/hash receipt,
  correctly refusing the prior HEAD. The final gate refresh is required.
- The formal source inventory now includes all four new production modules and
  names the codec/process witnesses. No new concurrent owner, durable checkpoint,
  retry protocol, lifecycle or Yarn topology is introduced. Parsing/JSON/raw
  replay are implementation-only coverage, not a product-model refinement claim.
  LcWatcher cursor/ack/crash models remain P7; bootstrap TLC parity proves the
  listed bounded checker corpus only. Native/TLC backend disagreements still fail.
- The 64 MiB native-line cap returns InvalidData. I/O failures propagate. A final
  line without LF is left unconsumed even if its JSON would otherwise parse.
  No arbitrary whole-session memory or wall-clock performance claim is made.
- --no-raw retains readable and sealed reasoning but same-provider reconstruction
  without raw needs the P6 synthesis path; this lowerer returns an error for it.
  Writer errors can leave a prefix in the caller's sink; transactional publication
  is the caller's responsibility. This module never places sessions itself.
- No cross-provider lowering, bxl CLI wiring, blob storage/fetching, sanitizer,
  durable watcher, compaction-history decryption, live paid endpoint acceptance,
  or real-user session validation is claimed. The existing CLI still reserves
  parse/lower commands until the bxl phases can wire those flows.
- P1 PR #1 remained OPEN/unmerged while P4 was verified. P4 was rebased to its
  latest branch commit bb87743; its PR is stacked on p1-bootstrap-ir. Rebase onto
  main remains conditional on P1 merging, per the assignment. No merge is performed.
- Source changes are committed. Generated target/, .bboxy/runs/test-current.json,
  the current native-resume log and verification/evidence/ archives stay local.
  The latter retain final source/model/tool hash receipts across target cleanup.
  Committed snapshots are p4-make-test.log and p4-resume-recorded.log; the canonical
  gate regenerates current receipts without altering those snapshots.
